note: A small pet shelter: kinds of things, lists, and commands that give back answers.
note: Run it with: py -3 imagination.py run examples/pets.imagine

a pet has:
  name (text)
  age (a number)
  tricks (a list of text)
and the universe said i love you

to start:
  set shelter to a list of pets
  add pet called with ("Rex", 3) to shelter
  add pet called with ("Mittens", 12) to shelter
  add pet called with ("Bubbles", 1) to shelter
  add "sit" to tricks of item 1 of shelter
  add "roll over" to tricks of item 1 of shelter

  for each pet in shelter:
    scrawl name of pet, " is ", age of pet, " and knows: ", tricks of pet

  scrawl "Oldest: ", name of oldest in shelter
  scrawl "Ages added up: ", total age of shelter
  set item 3 of shelter to pet called with ("Goldie", 2)
  remove item 2 from shelter
  scrawl "Left: ", names in shelter
  if names in shelter contains "Goldie": scrawl "Goldie found a home here."
and the universe said i love you

to pet called, given name (text) and age (a number), giving back a pet:
  set made to a new pet
  set name of made to name
  set age of made to age
  give back made
and the universe said i love you

to oldest in, given pets (a list of pets), giving back a pet:
  set best to item 1 of pets
  for each pet in pets:
    if age of pet is more than age of best: set best to pet
  give back best
and the universe said i love you

to total age of, given pets (a list of pets), giving back a number:
  set total to 0
  for each pet in pets: set total to total plus age of pet
  give back total
and the universe said i love you

to names in, given pets (a list of pets), giving back a list of text:
  set found to a list of text
  for each pet in pets: add name of pet to found
  give back found
and the universe said i love you
